From: OpenWrt EHR330 support <openwrt-devel@lists.openwrt.org>
Subject: [PATCH] mediatek: use BL31 key for tee_aes256 FIT images

The BL31 backend derives its key internally from the hardware platform key.
When an IV is carried in the signed FIT, no key node is needed in U-Boot's
control FDT.

--- a/boot/image-cipher.c
+++ b/boot/image-cipher.c
@@ -116,6 +116,12 @@ static int fit_image_setup_decrypt(struct image_cipher_info *info,
 		return -1;
 	}
 
+#ifndef USE_HOSTCC
+	if (CONFIG_IS_ENABLED(MTK_FW_ENCRYPT_VIA_BL31) && info->iv &&
+	    !strcmp(algo_name, "tee_aes256"))
+		return 0;
+#endif
+
 	/*
 	 * Search the cipher node in the u-boot fdt
 	 * the path should be: /cipher/key-<algo>-<key>-<iv>
